lone would give, and <strong>66 record highs</strong>, close to the 74 that chance alone would give. The 1940s hold the most record highs of any decade (51). Worcester's all-time high is 102\u00b0F, on July 4, 1911.","t_chg":"Worcester's nights have warmed. Its days have warmed since 1986.","p_chg":"Across 126 complete years: Worcester's average low has risen <strong class='sig'>+0.12\u00b0F per decade</strong> (95% range +0.04 to +0.21), about +1.6\u00b0F since 1895. Worcester's average high shows no clear change: \u22120.03\u00b0F per decade, a range (\u22120.10 to +0.05) that includes zero. <strong>The last 40 years tell a different story:</strong> since 1986, lows have risen <strong class='sig'>+1.02\u00b0F per decade</strong> (95% range +0.67 to +1.37) and highs have risen <strong class='sig'>+0.63\u00b0F per decade</strong> (95% range +0.27 to +1.00). The full record joins different observing sites over the years, and a move (for example, from the city to a cooler airport) can hide or exaggerate a long-run trend, so the recent decades are the clearer guide here.","t_mon":"Lows rose in 4 of 12 months. Highs rose in none; 3 months fell.","t_rain":"Worcester has gotten wetter","p_rain":"Worcester's yearly precipitation has risen <strong class='sig'>+1.09 inches per decade</strong> (95% range +0.74 to +1.44), about +14.2 inches since 1895. The 1991\u20132020 normal is 48.0 inches a year. The wettest year was 1972 (71.66 in); the driest, 1941 (27.92 in).","show_snow":true,"sig_bars":{"lo":true,"hi":false},"t_year":"2026 so far: 1 daily record high, no daily record lows"}}